"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIf I had to describe this book in one sentence, it would be: Who killed me?  \nAt first, the protagonist doesn't even realize he's dead, but once he does, he starts searching for the killer, convinced someone murdered him intentionally.  \n\nThe fresh part of this book is that the victim themselves deduces the killer's identity.  \nIt was a novel enough premise to make the book an interesting read.  \nHowever... somehow, it felt a bit lacking."